  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Public Support for Asian Elephant Conservation in Lao PDR with Friends of Wildlife Radio Program, Phase IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to, 1) Raise public awareness and knowledge of the status and threats to the Asian elephant, the Indochinese tiger and the five gibbon species in Lao PDR; 2) Build capacity of four target provincial radio stations in creating their own conservation radio programming that is sensitive to local contexts and dialects; 3) Reach a greater number of ethnic minorities by expanding the programs to Hmong and Khmu language radio stations; 4) Raise awareness about Asian elephant conservation among military personnel throughout the country; 5) Increase the listening audience by collaboration with a Lao telecommunications company; 6) Evaluate the effectiveness of past and current radio programs.</narrative>
  </description>
